<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baku</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baku is a city on the western shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a> and the capital of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. It was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in the early nineteenth century. From the late nineteenth century it became one of the world's leading oil-producing centres, an important part of the Russian Empire's industrial economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baku.jpg" alt="Baku" width="306" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See above. Compilation by Interfase · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baku_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
